cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use the Heat Transfer Virtual Lab in teaching or research, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Heat Transfer Virtual Lab: an open virtual laboratory for conduction, convection, radiation, phase change, heat exchangers and thermal systems"
abstract: >-
  Browser-based virtual laboratory with 18 heat transfer experiments: thermal
  conductivity of a metal rod, insulating powder, lagging and liquids; composite
  wall; transient conduction; pin fin; free convection, forced convection in a tube
  and cross flow over a cylinder; emissivity and the Stefan-Boltzmann constant; pool
  boiling and critical heat flux; filmwise and dropwise condensation; double-pipe
  heat exchanger; heat pipe; vapour compression refrigeration; and quenchant
  cooling-curve analysis with the ISO 9950 probe. Each experiment provides pre- and
  post-tests, theory with nomenclature and a narrated explainer, a safety briefing,
  do-it-yourself set-up with interlocks, a physics-based simulation with live
  thermal field and steady-state judgement, validation against correlations and
  handbook data with an energy balance, randomised numericals, a heat transfer data
  book, and a watermarked lab report with uncertainty analysis.
